Root cause found and fixed in:

`firmware/libopencm3-examples/examples/stm32/f4/stm32f4-discovery/usart_irq/usart_irq.c`

### Root cause
`USART2` peripheral interrupt generation was enabled (`RXNEIE`), but the corresponding **NVIC interrupt line was never enabled**.  
So RXNE flag sets in `USART_SR`, but `usart2_isr()` is never dispatched.

### Fix applied
Added NVIC enable inside `usart_setup()`:

```c
/* Enable USART2 NVIC line so RXNE/TXE can invoke usart2_isr(). */
nvic_enable_irq(NVIC_USART2_IRQ);
```

This connects the peripheral interrupt request to the Cortex-M interrupt controller, allowing RXNE/TXE events to call `usart2_isr()` and restore echo behavior.
